{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH visited Sarah as He had said</b> — in conception, \"as He had spoken\" — in childbirth; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 21:1). And \"פְּקִידָה\" means nothing other than remembrance and providential attention upon the one visited, as in \"פָּקֹד יִפְקֹד אֱלֹהִים אֶתְכֶם\" (Genesis 50:25), \"פָּקֹד פָּקַדְתִּי אֶתְכֶם וְאֶת הֶעָשׂוּי לָכֶם\" (Exodus 3:16), \"וַיִּפְקֹד שִׁמְשׁוֹן אֶת אִשְׁתּוֹ בִּגְדִי עִזִּים\" (Judges 15:1). So too here, \"וַה' פָּקַד אֶת שָׂרָה\" — He remembered Sarah and did for her as He had spoken. And likewise is the language for all the barren women who give birth: regarding Rachel, \"וַיִּזְכֹּר אֱלֹהִים אֶת רָחֵל\" (Genesis 30:22), and regarding Hannah, \"וַיִּזְכְּרֶהָ ה'\" (I Samuel 1:19). And thus they said: deposits of פְּקִידָה are like deposits of זִכְרוֹן (Rosh HaShanah 32)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:32:40.102609645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}